{"duration_api_ms":191429,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"32cd4b58-2dea-44c4-bed0-9e7f02104ff1","total_cost_usd":0.24397,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15894,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18039,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13335},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15894,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18039,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15894},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18039,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15894,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24397,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":13335,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional curve at the corner D≈3.3845 m, b=1.2, cone=70 deg, traced by flight-path angle from -1.5 to -3.567 deg. Flux runs 227k to 275k W/m2 and bondline temperature 418 to 391 K. Three limits box this corner in: the mass-fraction margin is only 0.0003 to 0.0007, the max_g margin is 0.0005 at gamma=-3.567, and the aero-surface hull rejects b>=1.21 at cone 70. Hypervolume gains have stalled (0.35365, 0.35505, 0.35531 over rounds 3 to 5). Other regions are dominated: small D or low b gives higher flux and higher bondline temperature.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-092723c51b5a: gamma=-3.567 gives g=11.994 (margin 0.0005) and mass margin 0.00026. D and gamma are both pinned at their limits.\",\"C-a565d31e5d1c to C-092723c51b5a: flux rises ~23k W/m2 per degree of steepening while bondline temperature falls ~9.7 K/deg. Any gamma between two front points lies on the non-dominated staircase.\",\"Mass margin vs D: 3.384 gives 7.4e-4, 3.3845 gives 4.4e-4, 3.3848 gives 2.6e-4. That is ~0.59 per m, consistent with mass ∝ D^2, so D can exceed 3.3848 by only ~4e-4 m.\",\"C-c050b796618a (D=3.3, b=1.17, cone 70): mass margin 0.049 and g=12.014 at gamma=-3.6, so b has little effect on area and g. Flux is 287k, worse than the D=3.38 curve.\",\"C-425c523a5086, C-5b57439845df, C-e605b64e0636, C-3d41ce848a30: b>=1.21 at cone 70 fails the cd_fore hull. The edge lies between b=1.2 and 1.21.\",\"C-c708a99f10f1, C-17a9b770e63c: cone<=67 at b=1.2 gives a negative fore-cone length, so cone 70 is both the limit and the optimum.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This relies on the data plus prior Sutton-Graves reasoning. Flux falls with nose radius (bD) and with ballistic coefficient, and bondline temperature falls with heat load, so the best designs have the largest D that the mass fraction allows. A larger b and cone 70 give the flattest forebody with the least area per D^2. Steeper entry lowers bondline temperature at the cost of flux and g, so the corner is set by mass fraction, max_g and the hull. The remaining gains are small: (1) probing b just above 1.2, where a 0.4 to 1 percent larger nose radius trims flux by ~0.2 to 0.5 percent; (2) pushing gamma to the g limit; (3) filling gaps along the curve, since every interpolated gamma is non-dominated; (4) two cheap probes of whether lower b or smaller D lowers g enough to allow steeper gamma.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The hull edge for b at cone 70 is unknown, so b=1.202 to 1.208 may return an extrapolation failure. Mass margin at D=3.385 is ~1e-4, so it may flip to infeasible. Predicted g near the limit is uncertain by about 0.01 g. Interpolated flux and temperature values are linear and should be accurate to about 0.3 percent. The two exploration probes are expected to be dominated.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-092723c51b5a\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to the g limit: g slope is ~1.68 per deg, so gamma=-3.570 gives g≈11.999.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the corner of the front by 0.003 deg. It may cross the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-092723c51b5a\",\"rationale\":\"Test slightly larger D. Mass margin extrapolates to ~1.4e-4 at D=3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction edge precisely.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-092723c51b5a\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the hull edge with a small b increase. A larger nose radius lowers flux, and a flatter cap reduces area.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.202,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A small step above b=1.2 is likely inside the hull and may improve both objectives slightly.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-092723c51b5a\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the hull edge with a slightly larger b step.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.204,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps where the cd_fore hull edge lies between 1.2 and 1.21.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-092723c51b5a\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the hull edge closer to the failed b=1.21.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.206,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Continues the hull-edge scan. The failed b=1.21 was at D=3.38, so the edge is ambiguous.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-092723c51b5a\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the hull edge just below the known failure at 1.21.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.208,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.15,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the largest usable b. It is likely to fail the hull, but success would give the best flux.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Densify the shallow end of the front between -1.5 and -1.575 (linear interpolation).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227840,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.38,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front staircase and adds a small hypervolume gain.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -1.575 and -1.7.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.63},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229840,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.75,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap with a low-risk point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the wide gap between -1.75 and -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.87},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":234900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the largest gap in the front at the shallow end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.2 and -2.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243260,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.41,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.43 and -2.55.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249040,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.06,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.625 and -2.69.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.66},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":252860,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.03,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.69 and -2.81.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254970,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.94,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -2.81 and -2.95.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258550,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.16,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -3.05 and -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.12},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263810,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -3.3 and -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.36},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269630,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.18,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap. g is about 11.65, safely feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-05012f86327d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between -3.42 and -3.48.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271755,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.27,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap near the g limit. g is about 11.80, still feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Exploration: lower b (1.1) at slightly smaller D to test whether g drops enough to allow steeper gamma. The C-c050b796618a data hinted at a slight g reduction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the sensitivity of g and area to b, and whether a different corner exists. It is likely dominated but informative.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-12721d8cb32a\",\"rationale\":\"Exploration: smaller D=3.2 at b=1.2, cone 70 to see how g and bondline temperature vary with D at gamma=-3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":294500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether reduced D lowers g, which would relax the gamma cap. Most likely dominated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":155081,"type":"result","duration_ms":191464,"uuid":"3fdf2d18-9e7e-4ba3-ab9a-b4bd8739abc8","ttft_stream_ms":1338,"time_to_request_ms":31,"first_content_frame_ms":1338,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
